{"nodes": [{"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "label": "MOOC Lecture 12: zkEVM Design, Optimization, and Applications (Scroll)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zkevm", "label": "zkEVM", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proves batches of EVM transactions at the bytecode level so Solidity developers never write circuits and cross-app composability is preserved; became practical (~3 orders of magnitude) through flexible arithmetization (custom gates + lookups), hardware-accelerated provers, and recursive aggregation. Classified as language-, bytecode-, or consensus-level depending on compatibility depth."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zk_rollup", "label": "zk-Rollup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Layer-2 executes transactions off-chain and posts one succinct validity proof to L1, so L1 verifies a proof instead of re-executing every transaction."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_plonkish_arithmetization", "label": "Plonkish Arithmetization", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen over R1CS because custom gates plus case-switch selectors handle the EVM's dynamic execution trace (open different opcode constraints per step) and lookups give cheap range proofs, RAM read/write consistency, and linking between subcircuits."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_custom_gates", "label": "Custom Gates", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_lookup_argument", "label": "Lookup Argument / Lookup Tables", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prove a tuple belongs to a table: brute-force tables give cheap range and bitwise checks, dynamically generated tables give RAM consistency and hash outsourcing (Keccak table), and lookups are the glue connecting the zkEVM's subcircuits."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_halo2_kzg", "label": "Halo2-KZG Proof System", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Halo2's Plonkish front end with KZG (BN curve) replacing IPA/Pasta so proofs verify cheaply on Ethereum precompiles; used in both Scroll layers, with thin few-column aggregation tables and Poseidon-for-inner / Keccak-for-outer Fiat-Shamir hashing."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_evm_circuit", "label": "EVM Circuit (State Machine Circuit)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-step witness = step context + one-hot case switch + opcode-specific cells; 256-bit words split into 8-bit limbs; ~100 columns and 2000+ custom gates."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_aggregation_circuit", "label": "Proof Aggregation Circuit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Second-layer circuit proving all subcircuit proofs valid so only one proof is verified on L1; kept very thin (few columns) since verification cost is linear in columns."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_random_linear_combination_encoding", "label": "Random Linear Combination (RLC) Encoding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compresses 32 8-bit limbs of an EVM word (and multi-cell lookup tuples) into one field element; sound only if the randomness is derived after the limbs are fixed, forcing the multi-phase Challenge API and pushing all subcircuits into one super circuit."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_gpu_prover_acceleration", "label": "GPU Prover Acceleration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "MSM, NTT and quotient kernels parallelize well (30s EVM-circuit proofs), but then witness generation and CPU-to-GPU data copy dominate - a long-tail bottleneck that pure kernel acceleration cannot fix; peak memory cut from ~1TB to ~300GB CPU / 8GB GPU."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_proof_of_exploit", "label": "Proof of Exploit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Make the transaction a private input: prove 'I know a transaction moving the state root to one where your balance is zero' - demonstrating a bug without revealing it."}, {"id": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zk_oracle", "label": "zk-Oracle / zk Coprocessor Attestation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Ye Zhang", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trustlessly read historical on-chain data via zkEVM state proofs, compute over it off-chain, and verify the result on-chain (e.g. Axiom)."}], "edges": [{"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zkevm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zk_rollup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_plonkish_arithmetization", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_custom_gates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_lookup_argument", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_halo2_kzg", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_evm_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_aggregation_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_random_linear_combination_encoding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_gpu_prover_acceleration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_proof_of_exploit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript", "target": "references_mooc_lecture12_transcript_zk_oracle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "references/mooc/lecture12/transcript.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.